    "policy": "Public actions only. First cask is manually distilled in both arms. Thereafter one arm manually starts/stops/fills; the other explicitly reserves exactly one next cask per production request. Both hold at most two aging casks and bottle at age six to the same brand at standard price. Decisions and offers pause simulation until handled. Each extraction step uses one clock callback; no instant distillation or modified cash. Extra bourbon cost is protected equally in both arms. Non-log runtime state is compared every month.",
    "limits": "Matched policy, not a claim that automation increases demand or production. One recipe per seed, cycling early30/mid65/late99 and both casks; two repeat-seed recipes. Pauses and UI scheduling are covered by separate tests.",
